  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'State the laws of reflection and refraction and write down at least one application of each. (3 marks)', 'Laws of reflection: (1) the angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection; (2) the incident ray, the reflected ray and the normal at the point of incidence all lie in the same plane.
Laws of refraction: (1) the incident ray, the refracted ray and the normal lie in the same plane; (2) Snell''s law - for two given media, sin i / sin r is constant (the refractive index of the second medium relative to the first).
Applications: reflection - plane and curved mirrors, periscopes, rear-view mirrors, dentist''s and ENT head mirrors; refraction - lenses in spectacles, cameras, microscopes and the eye; also total internal reflection in optical fibres and endoscopes.', null, '[{"point": "Reflection: angle of incidence = angle of reflection; incident ray, reflected ray and normal lie in the same plane", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Refraction: incident ray, refracted ray and normal lie in one plane; Snell''s law sin i/sin r = constant (refractive index)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Applications: reflection - mirrors, periscope, rear-view mirror, dental mirror; refraction - lenses in spectacles, cameras, microscopes, optical fibre/endoscope", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
