  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'State the specific function of each of the following: (i) pulmonary artery, (ii) glomerulus, (iii) islets of Langerhans, (iv) patella, (v) gall bladder, (vi) duodenum. (3 marks)', '(a) Pulmonary artery - carries deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs for oxygenation.
(b) Glomerulus - a knot of capillaries in Bowman''s capsule that filters blood under pressure (ultrafiltration), forming the glomerular filtrate - the first step in urine formation.
(c) Islets of Langerhans - endocrine cells of the pancreas: β cells secrete insulin (lowers blood glucose) and α cells secrete glucagon (raises it).
(d) Patella (knee cap) - a sesamoid bone that protects the front of the knee joint and improves the leverage of the quadriceps tendon.
(e) Gall bladder - stores and concentrates bile made by the liver and releases it into the duodenum after a fatty meal.
(f) Duodenum - first part of the small intestine; receives bile and pancreatic juice, neutralises the acid from the stomach and carries out most chemical digestion.', null, '[{"point": "(a) Pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs; (b) glomerulus filters blood (ultrafiltration) to form glomerular filtrate in the nephron", "marks": 1}, {"point": "(c) Islets of Langerhans secrete insulin (β cells) and glucagon (α cells) to control blood sugar; (d) patella (knee cap) protects the knee joint and increases the leverage of the quadriceps", "marks": 1}, {"point": "(e) Gall bladder stores and concentrates bile and releases it into the duodenum; (f) duodenum receives bile and pancreatic juice and is the main site of chemical digestion (neutralises stomach acid)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
