  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Hepatitis B is a serious public health problem. Describe its causative agent, modes of transmission and preventive measures. (3 marks)', 'Causative agent: the hepatitis B virus (HBV), a DNA virus that attacks liver cells. It can cause acute hepatitis (jaundice, fatigue, dark urine) and, especially when acquired in infancy, lifelong chronic infection leading to cirrhosis and liver cancer.
Modes of transmission: through infected blood and body fluids - transfusion of unscreened blood, unsafe injections and sharing needles, unsterile instruments (tattooing, ear-piercing), sexual contact, from an infected mother to her baby at birth, and sharing razors or toothbrushes. It is not spread by food, water or casual contact.
Preventive measures: hepatitis B vaccination (birth dose within 24 hours plus the infant schedule, and vaccination of health workers); screening of blood donors and pregnant women, with hepatitis B immunoglobulin and vaccine for babies of infected mothers; safe injection practice, sterilisation of instruments and proper sharps disposal; using condoms; not sharing razors or needles; health education.', null, '[{"point": "Caused by the hepatitis B virus (a DNA virus) that infects the liver; can cause acute hepatitis, chronic infection, cirrhosis and liver cancer", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Transmission: blood and blood products, unsafe injections/needle sharing, sexual contact, mother to child at birth, sharing razors/toothbrushes; not by food or water", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Prevention: hepatitis B vaccine (birth dose and infant schedule, health workers), screening of blood and pregnant women, safe injections and sterilisation, condoms, not sharing razors, HBIG for exposed newborns", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
